description:
Design a digital circuit that combines a 4-bit shift register with a 2-bit D flip-flop. On every rising edge of the clock signal, the circuit shifts in a new data bit `d` into the shift register, while the most significant bit of the shift register is stored in the flip-flop. The output `q` corresponds to the second bit of the flip-flop, effectively capturing and outputting specific data from the shifting process.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output q
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output q
);reg [3:0] shift_reg;
    reg [1:0] flip_flop;

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        shift_reg <= {shift_reg[2:0], d};
        flip_flop <= {flip_flop[0], shift_reg[3]};
    end

    assign q = flip_flop[1];

endmodule

