Design a 4-bit modulo-16 adder. This module takes two 4-bit inputs, A and B, and computes their sum, Y. If the resulting sum exceeds 15 (i.e., modulo 16), it wraps around by subtracting 16. This effectively implements behavior similar to a finite state machine operating within a cyclic range of values from 0 to 15.
