description:
Design a ring counter with a configurable number of flip-flops, defined by the parameter 'm'. The counter circulates its state by shifting the bits on each clock cycle, allowing the highest bit to wrap around to the lowest position. When all bits are set to high, it resets to a state of all low bits. The output represents the current state of the counter, which will produce a repeating sequence of bit patterns as determined by the number of flip-flops.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [m-1:0] out
);

