Design a display controller that drives a 7-segment display based on 16-bits of input data and a clock signal. It scans four 4-bit segments from the memory data and controls which segment is active using a divided clock signal, allowing one segment to be displayed at a time. The corresponding segments are activated by setting the appropriate outputs for the anodes, while a separate process translates each 4-bit value into the correct cathode patterns for the 7-segment display. The module also includes a reset capability to ensure proper operation.
